<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.14.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01506</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.14.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>701bdbda-dbff-4f63-ae48-44c187a9b614</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><section id="sect-00002"><exercise id="_91b86a46-3b99-4625-ad43-24e8495050c2" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00001"><para id="para-00001">Functions <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>e</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> are given below. Which functions are linear?<emphasis>Select the three</emphasis> answers
          that apply.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00001"><para id="para-00002">Try again. Revisit activity 5.14.1. 
    </para><para id="para-00003">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_7e5c2385-363a-4bc2-b500-8771bcfa0add" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00002"><para id="para-00004">Functions <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>e</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> are given below. Which functions are exponential?<emphasis>Select the two</emphasis> answers that apply.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00002"><para id="para-00005">Try again. Revisit activities 5.14.1.</para><para id="para-00006">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>e</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="c560e6be-58d4-4a05-94bd-22d2063c7a09" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00003"><para id="para-00007">Here are 4 equations defining 4 different functions, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. List them in order of increasing rate of change. That is, start with the one that grows the slowest and end with the one that grows the quickest. </para>
          <para id="para-00008"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00009"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00010"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00011"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00012">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00013">Option 1: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00014">Option 2: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00015">Option 3: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>,<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00016">Option 4: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00003"><para id="para-00017">Try again. Revisit activity 5.14.3. 
    </para><para id="para-00018">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise></section><para id="para-00019">Use the given information for problems 4 – 6. Technology is required. Function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is defined by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>,
  and function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is defined by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1.1</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
<table class="os-raise-doubleheadertable" id="table-00001">
  <tgroup cols="3"><tbody><row>
      <entry><emphasis>
     </emphasis> </entry><entry><emphasis>
        <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>
     </emphasis> </entry><entry><emphasis>
        <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>
     </emphasis> </entry></row>
  <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        1
     </emphasis> </entry><entry/>
      <entry/>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        5
     </emphasis> </entry><entry/>
      <entry/>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        10
     </emphasis> </entry><entry/>
      <entry/>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        20
     </emphasis> </entry><entry/>
      <entry/>
    </row>
  </tbody></tgroup></table>
<section id="sect-00003"><exercise id="_04eb6bed-b602-46eb-95d3-8bcd36a15239" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00004"><para id="para-00020">Which values will complete the table for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
      <para id="para-00021">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00022">8, 11, 14, 17</para><para id="para-00023">8, 20, 35, 65</para><para id="para-00024">3, 15, 30, 60</para><para id="para-00025">8, 15, 30, 60</para></problem><solution id="sol-00004"><para id="para-00026">Try again. Revisit activities 5.14.2.</para><para id="para-00027">The correct answer is 8, 20, 35, 65.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="f8c05a03-2554-4d04-9263-88fb53e061e5" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00005"><para id="para-00028">Which of the following sets of values will complete the table for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
      <para id="para-00029">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00030">8, 20, 35, 65</para><para id="para-00031">1.1, 5.5, 10.10, 20.20</para><para id="para-00032">1.1, 1.6, 2.59, 6.73</para><para id="para-00033">1.1, 1.21, 1.33, 1.46</para></problem><solution id="sol-00005"><para id="para-00034">Try again. Revisit activity 5.14.2. 
    </para><para id="para-00035">The correct answer is 1.1, 1.6, 2.59, 6.73.</para></solution></exercise>
     <exercise id="_02e97ed5-02f5-4a77-affa-d83b7b8287f2" class="multiple-choice">
      <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00036">________ is a linear function.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00006"><para id="para-00037">Try again. Revisit activities 5.14.3.</para><para id="para-00038">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is a linear function.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="e02206a3-611d-4186-b1af-4a9fffd02411" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00007"><para id="para-00039">________ is an exponential function.</para>
        </problem><solution id="sol-00007"><para id="para-00040">Try again. Revisit activities 5.14.3.</para><para id="para-00041">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is an exponential function.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_242f0919-e0cc-46f6-906d-e500e5353468" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00008"><para id="para-00042">Functions <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> are given by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1.05</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. As <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> increases from
          0, __________ reaches 30 first.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00008"><para id="para-00043">Try again. Revisit activity 5.14.3. 
    </para><para id="para-00044">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="a529212b-5978-4fb5-89a6-8c64dc239be0" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00009"><para id="para-00045">Functions <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> are given by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1.05</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. As <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math><emphasis>
         </emphasis> increases from 0, __________ reaches 100 first.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00009"><para id="para-00046">Try again. Revisit activity 5.14.3. 
    </para><para id="para-00047">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_274bbeb1-10b8-4f67-8aba-fcc075b326c9" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00010"><para id="para-00048">The functions <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> are defined by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>33</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1.2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>. Which function
          eventually grows faster, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>? Explain how you know.</para>
      <para id="para-00049">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00050"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> grows faster because 8 is greater than 1.2.</para><para id="para-00051"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> grows faster because 33 is greater than 2.</para><para id="para-00052"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> grows faster because it is a linear function.</para><para id="para-00053"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> grows faster because it is an exponential function.</para></problem><solution id="sol-00010"><para id="para-00054">Try again. Revisit activity 5.14.4. 
    </para><para id="para-00055">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> grows faster because it is an exponential function.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_479162ef-4347-4bc2-aa36-7089c8ada675" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00011"><para id="para-00056">A line segment of length <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>l</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is scaled by a factor of 1.5 to produce a segment with length <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. The new
          segment is then scaled by a factor of 1.5 to give a segment of length <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.
          
          What scale factor takes the segment of length <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>l</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> to the segment of length <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>? 
      </para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00011"><para id="para-00057">Try again. Revisit activities 5.14.1.</para><para id="para-00058">The correct answer is 2.25.</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>